# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Determine stabilizers to measure {#6-determine-stabilizers-to-measure}"
msgstr "6. Tentukan stabilizer yang akan diukur {#6-determine-stabilizers-to-measure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To test the performance of the error detection we will estimate the fidelity of the stabilizer state, $|\\psi\\rangle = U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, that the circuit ideally prepares against the noisy state, $\\rho$, the hardware actually outputs. The projector onto the pure stabilizer state, $|\\psi\\rangle$, is defined to be the uniform average over the $2^n$ elements of its stabilizer group $\\mathcal{S}$:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menguji performa deteksi error, kita akan mengestimasi fidelity state stabilizer, $|\\psi\\rangle = U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, yang idealnya disiapkan circuit, terhadap state ber-noise, $\\rho$, yang sebenarnya dihasilkan hardware. Proyektor ke state stabilizer murni, $|\\psi\\rangle$, didefinisikan sebagai rata-rata seragam atas $2^n$ elemen grup stabilizer-nya $\\mathcal{S}$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi| = \\frac{1}{2^n}\\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} G$$\n"
msgstr "$$|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi| = \\frac{1}{2^n}\\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} G$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plugging this into the fidelity equation, we see that the fidelity of noisy state, $\\rho$, is equivalent to the average expectation value of all stabilizers, $G \\in \\mathcal{S}$, with respect to $\\rho$:\n"
msgstr "Dengan memasukkan ini ke persamaan fidelity, kita melihat bahwa fidelity state ber-noise, $\\rho$, sama dengan rata-rata expectation value semua stabilizer, $G \\in \\mathcal{S}$, terhadap $\\rho$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$F = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi|) = \\mathrm{Tr}({\\frac{1}{2^n}\\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} \\rho G}) = \\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho G) = \\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} \\langle G \\rangle_\\rho$$\n"
msgstr "$$F = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi|) = \\mathrm{Tr}({\\frac{1}{2^n}\\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} \\rho G}) = \\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho G) = \\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} \\langle G \\rangle_\\rho$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For larger problems, measuring (or even enumerating) all $2^n$ stabilizers is infeasible, so fidelity is often estimated by measuring a random sample of stabilizers. Sampling $M$ stabilizers $G_1, \\ldots, G_M$ uniformly at random from $\\mathcal{S}$ gives an unbiased estimator of the fidelity, $\\hat F_M$,\n"
msgstr "Untuk masalah yang lebih besar, mengukur (bahkan sekadar mengenumerasi) semua $2^n$ stabilizer tidak layak dilakukan, sehingga fidelity sering diestimasi dengan mengukur sampel acak stabilizer. Mengambil sampel $M$ stabilizer $G_1, \\ldots, G_M$ secara seragam acak dari $\\mathcal{S}$ menghasilkan estimator fidelity yang tak bias, $\\hat F_M$,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\\hat F_M = \\frac{1}{M} \\sum_{i=1}^M \\langle G_i \\rangle_\\rho$$\n"
"For this experiment we will make the circuit much deeper to enhance the effect of gate noise, and we will add checks to every qubit with a neighboring ancilla qubit. While there are more sophisticated ways to sample stabilizers to estimate fidelity, in this example we will sample $100$ stabilizers with uniform probability.\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\\hat F_M = \\frac{1}{M} \\sum_{i=1}^M \\langle G_i \\rangle_\\rho$$\n"
"Untuk eksperimen ini kita akan membuat circuit jauh lebih dalam untuk memperkuat efek noise Gate, dan kita akan menambahkan check ke setiap qubit yang punya qubit ancilla bertetangga. Meskipun ada cara yang lebih canggih untuk mengambil sampel stabilizer guna mengestimasi fidelity, dalam contoh ini kita akan mengambil sampel $100$ stabilizer dengan probabilitas seragam.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. Find good checks for the whole state {#7-find-good-checks-for-the-whole-state}"
msgstr "7. Temukan check yang bagus untuk seluruh state {#7-find-good-checks-for-the-whole-state}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We find one set of checks for the deep circuit exactly as in step 5. Since the checks read only their ancillas, the same checked circuit serves every sampled stabilizer. The returned circuits measure only the check ancillas, so we will add the payload measurements in the next step.\n"
msgstr "Kita menemukan satu set check untuk circuit dalam persis seperti di langkah 5. Karena check hanya membaca ancilla-nya, circuit ber-check yang sama bisa dipakai untuk setiap stabilizer yang disampel. Circuit yang dikembalikan hanya mengukur ancilla check, jadi kita akan menambahkan pengukuran payload di langkah berikutnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "8. Sample from the noisy circuit {#8-sample-from-the-noisy-circuit}"
msgstr "8. Lakukan sampling dari circuit ber-noise {#8-sample-from-the-noisy-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We sample every variant, from the bare payload to the circuit with all ``7`` checks, for each sampled stabilizer. The variant with zero checks is the bare payload with the same measurements, so it serves as the noisy reference. Instead of appending the basis rotation of every stabilizer to a copy of every variant, we let [samplomatic](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic) choose the measurement basis at sampling time. For each variant we:\n"
msgstr "Kita melakukan sampling setiap varian, dari payload polos hingga circuit dengan semua ``7`` check, untuk setiap stabilizer yang disampel. Varian dengan nol check adalah payload polos dengan pengukuran yang sama, sehingga berfungsi sebagai referensi ber-noise. Alih-alih menambahkan rotasi basis setiap stabilizer ke salinan setiap varian, kita membiarkan [samplomatic](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic) memilih basis pengukuran pada saat sampling. Untuk setiap varian kita:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure the payload and group the terminal measurements into a box with samplomatic's boxing pass manager. The box carries a ``ChangeBasis`` annotation, so ``build`` returns a template circuit whose basis-changing gates are parameterized, along with a samplex that computes the parameters for a requested basis.\n"
msgstr "Mengukur payload dan mengelompokkan pengukuran terminal ke dalam sebuah box dengan boxing pass manager milik samplomatic. Box tersebut membawa anotasi ``ChangeBasis``, sehingga ``build`` mengembalikan circuit template yang Gate pengubah basisnya diparameterisasi, beserta samplex yang menghitung parameter untuk basis yang diminta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add the template and samplex to a ``QuantumProgram``. The samplex takes one measurement basis per qubit in the box, in ascending physical order, encoded as $I=0$, $Z=1$, $X=2$, $Y=3$. Passing an array of bases with a leading axis of length ``100`` makes a single item measure all ``100`` stabilizers: the payload in each stabilizer's basis and the ancillas in $Z$. A qubit outside a stabilizer's support is also measured in $Z$, and its bit is ignored when the stabilizer's expectation value is computed.\n"
msgstr "Menambahkan template dan samplex ke sebuah ``QuantumProgram``. Samplex menerima satu basis pengukuran per qubit di dalam box, dalam urutan fisik menaik, dengan encoding $I=0$, $Z=1$, $X=2$, $Y=3$. Memberikan array basis dengan axis pertama sepanjang ``100`` membuat satu item mengukur semua ``100`` stabilizer: payload dalam basis tiap stabilizer dan ancilla dalam $Z$. Qubit di luar support sebuah stabilizer juga diukur dalam $Z$, dan bit-nya diabaikan saat expectation value stabilizer dihitung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ``Executor`` primitive from ``qiskit-ibm-runtime`` runs the whole program in one job. Given an ``AerSimulator`` in place of a QPU it runs locally on that simulator, so we hand it one with the same depolarizing gate noise we used to find the checks, and use the stabilizer method since all of the circuits are Clifford. Qiskit Aer is needed only to build this simulator: the local mode takes the seed from the ``Executor`` options but ignores their ``noise_model``, so the noise must be set on the simulator itself. Passing a QPU backend instead would run the same program on hardware. Once the simulations are complete, we will calculate the postselection rate and expectation values to get a feel for how well the error detection worked before visualizing the data.\n"
msgstr "Primitive ``Executor`` dari ``qiskit-ibm-runtime`` menjalankan seluruh program dalam satu job. Jika diberi ``AerSimulator`` sebagai pengganti QPU, ia berjalan secara lokal pada simulator tersebut, jadi kita memberinya simulator dengan depolarizing noise Gate yang sama dengan yang kita pakai untuk menemukan check, dan memakai metode stabilizer karena semua circuit adalah Clifford. Qiskit Aer hanya dibutuhkan untuk membangun simulator ini: mode lokal mengambil seed dari opsi ``Executor`` tetapi mengabaikan ``noise_model`` mereka, jadi noise harus ditetapkan pada simulator itu sendiri. Memberikan Backend QPU sebagai gantinya akan menjalankan program yang sama di hardware. Setelah simulasi selesai, kita akan menghitung postselection rate dan expectation value untuk mendapat gambaran seberapa baik deteksi error bekerja sebelum memvisualisasikan datanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "9. Postselect checked circuit samples {#9-postselect-checked-circuit-samples}"
msgstr "9. Postselect sampel circuit ber-check {#9-postselect-checked-circuit-samples}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this package a check is implemented using entangling gates between one ancilla qubit and one target qubit. Each ancilla starts in $|0\\rangle$, so $Z_\\text{anc}$ stabilizes its input state. Forward propagating $Z_\\text{anc}$ from the beginning of the ancilla through the entire checked circuit yields $Z_\\text{anc}$ times a stabilizer of the prepared state, so the check passes if the ancilla bit is $0$. A sample is kept if every check passes.\n"
msgstr "Dalam package ini, sebuah check diimplementasikan menggunakan Gate entangling antara satu qubit ancilla dan satu qubit target. Setiap ancilla dimulai dalam $|0\\rangle$, sehingga $Z_\\text{anc}$ menstabilkan state inputnya. Merambatkan $Z_\\text{anc}$ maju dari awal ancilla melalui seluruh circuit ber-check menghasilkan $Z_\\text{anc}$ dikali sebuah stabilizer dari state yang disiapkan, sehingga check lolos jika bit ancilla bernilai $0$. Sebuah sampel dipertahankan jika setiap check lolos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The checked circuits measure the ancillas into the ``checks_c`` register, so a sample is kept if every bit of that register is ``0``. In general, the ``get_postselection_method`` method of the ``CheckedCircuit`` instances output from ``add_pauli_checks`` maps a shot's bitstring to the syndrome of every check at once; for checks found for the stabilizers of the prepared state, each syndrome is just its ancilla bit, so we read the register directly.\n"
msgstr "Circuit ber-check mengukur ancilla ke register ``checks_c``, sehingga sebuah sampel dipertahankan jika setiap bit register tersebut bernilai ``0``. Secara umum, method ``get_postselection_method`` dari instance ``CheckedCircuit`` yang dihasilkan ``add_pauli_checks`` memetakan bitstring sebuah shot ke syndrome setiap check sekaligus; untuk check yang ditemukan bagi stabilizer state yang disiapkan, setiap syndrome hanyalah bit ancilla-nya, jadi kita membaca register secara langsung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the chart, we see that adding more checks causes the postselection rate to go down. While the goal of error detection is to catch as many errors as possible, as postselection rate goes down more shots may be required to achieve some target accuracy. If the postselection rate drops too low, the number of shots needed to collect one logical sample may become prohibitive. In this example, the postselection rate seems to converge, implying that additional checks are contributing less additional detection capability. Although adding more Pauli checks generally provides greater error detection capability, it comes at a cost of increased circuit depth and an increase in sampling cost.\n"
msgstr "Pada chart, kita melihat bahwa menambah lebih banyak check menyebabkan postselection rate turun. Meskipun tujuan deteksi error adalah menangkap error sebanyak mungkin, saat postselection rate turun, mungkin dibutuhkan lebih banyak shot untuk mencapai akurasi target tertentu. Jika postselection rate turun terlalu rendah, jumlah shot yang dibutuhkan untuk mengumpulkan satu sampel logis bisa menjadi terlalu besar. Dalam contoh ini, postselection rate tampak konvergen, yang menyiratkan bahwa check tambahan memberi kontribusi kemampuan deteksi tambahan yang makin kecil. Meskipun menambah lebih banyak Pauli check umumnya memberi kemampuan deteksi error yang lebih besar, hal itu datang dengan biaya kedalaman circuit yang meningkat dan biaya sampling yang bertambah.\n"

